        "text": "<thinking> To implement the file `start_oauth_login.py` that starts an OAuth or OIDC authorization-code login, I need to choose a concrete external provider and use its identifiable code. For this task, I will use Google as the external provider, as it is a commonly used OAuth provider. I will import the necessary modules from the `google-auth` library, which is the official Google Auth library for Python. This will make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
